An Azure landing zone is a standardized foundation for hosting workloads in Azure. It establishes core governance, identity, networking, security, and management capabilities before application teams begin deploying workloads.

A landing zone commonly addresses:

* Management groups
* Subscriptions
* Identity
* Networking
* Security
* Governance
* Monitoring
* Resource organization

For example, an enterprise migrating hundreds of applications to Azure can establish a standardized landing-zone architecture before onboarding individual application teams.

A real-life use case is a multinational organization creating a consistent Azure foundation across business units while allowing individual teams to deploy their workloads within approved boundaries.

Landing zones accelerate cloud adoption while reducing architectural inconsistency and governance problems.
